insert into public.event_editions (edition_id,series_id,year,edition_label,start_date,end_date,date_precision,venue,city,country,disciplines,status,status_note,notes,sources,confidence) values ('world-snowboarding-championships-sims--1987','world-snowboarding-championships-sims',1987,'1987 World Snowboarding Championships',null,null,null,'Breckenridge Ski Resort','Breckenridge','USA',array['halfpipe','giant-slalom','slalom']::text[],'held',null,'DATE CONFLICT. The Snowboarder/TransWorld 1980s timeline and Paul Alden''s obituaries put the second Breckenridge Worlds in March 1987 - specifically, NASBA was formed on 8 March 1987, ''the day after'' the championships ended, which implies the event finished 7 March 1987. TransWorld''s halfpipe history instead dates the 1987 Breckenridge World Championships to 2-5 April 1987 and calls its pipe (about 200 feet long with near-vertical six-foot walls) the best in snowboarding to that point. Dates left null. Jose Fernandes is reported to have won the giant slalom on an asymmetrical board (snowboarding8090.com) - not corroborated, no result row written. Craig Kelly''s published timeline lists ''Swatch World Championships'' results for 1987 and 1988, which is the strongest indication that the Breckenridge Worlds carried Swatch''s name.',array['https://www.snowboarder.com/news/snowboard-history-timeline-part-21980s','https://snowbrains.com/snowboarding-pioneer-paul-alden-dies-aged-89/','https://www.tetonvalleynews.net/townnews/sport/a-founding-figure-of-organized-competitive-snowboarding-has-passed/article_db455d7f-ed68-46f1-a971-050e55e36410.amp.html','https://www.snowboarder.com/transworld-snowboarding-archive/a-complete-history-of-the-snowboard-halfpipe','https://snowboarding8090.com/history/','https://www.snowboarder.com/transworld-snowboarding-archive/three-decades-transworld-snowboarding-part-1-1987-1996']::text[],'likely')
